; Autoload scene for the VGCP Server (Video Game Control Protocol).
;
; SUPERSEDED and not maintained: the supported wiring is `vgcp_server::on_stage_init`
; (see INTEGRATION.md). Use this scene only instead of that call, never with it: two
; servers would contend for the same port, and the second one quits the game.
;
; The root node's `type` is the custom class registered by the gdext extension
; (`VgcpServer`). Because GDExtension classes are registered before autoloads
; load, Godot resolves this type at scene-load time, with no GDScript involved.
;
; Install: copy this file to `autoload/vgcp_server.tscn` in your Godot project, then
; add to that project's `project.godot`:
;
;   [autoload]
;   VgcpServer="*res://autoload/vgcp_server.tscn"
;
; The leading "*" makes it a singleton autoload available in every scene.
;
; No `uid="..."` is hand-written here: a fake base31 string would make Godot warn and
; reassign a fresh UID on first import anyway. Godot generates a real one when it saves
; this scene (a `.tscn.uid` sidecar / inline uid). Autoloads resolve by path regardless.

[gd_scene format=3]

[node name="VgcpServer" type="VgcpServer"]
